WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.140
A ladder leans against a smooth wall,
its foot resting on rough ground.

2
00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:10.000
Someone starts to climb, rung
by rung, higher and higher.

3
00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:13.290
So why is a slip more
likely the higher you go?

4
00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:15.610
Does your weight press the foot down less?

5
00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:17.670
Or does it make no difference?

6
00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:20.970
In this mission, you'll mark
every force on the ladder:

7
00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:26.140
its weight, the wall's reaction, and a
normal reaction and friction at the ground.

8
00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:30.760
You'll find a moment using the perpendicular
distance to a force's line of action.

9
00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:35.060
Then you'll resolve, take moments,
and use limiting friction:

10
00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:37.240
F equals mu R.

11
00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:41.580
Your mission: explain why a ladder is
more likely to slip when you're up near

12
00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:42.370
the top.
